{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509970-necromancy-ritual-v20-masquerade","id":1509970,"title":"Necromancy Ritual - V20 Masquerade","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-28T11:10:29-07:00","id":1509970,"title":"Necromancy Ritual - V20 Masquerade","content":"Hi All,<br /> in Rites of Blood, there is a Ritual forth level named: \u2018Summon Ethereal Horde\u2019<br /> copied the description for quick reference<br /> ********<br /> System: At the end of the chant, if the ritual is successful, the number of successes rolled determines how many drones (mindless ghosts, rather than full-blown wraiths) the Necromancer can summon. These ghosts appear as ethereal images of warriors long dead. Although they can not materialize fully in the physical world, they can use their own powers to hurl objects or frighten away attackers, in defense of the Necromancer. The ghosts return to their rest at the next sunrise.<br /> ********<br /> <br /> any suggestion how to apply according to your view?<br /> as per my view, considering the level, an the horde will try to defend the Necromancer in any potential risk situation.<br /> i.e. during a melee, Necromancer agains an enemy, the horde will penalize the attack of the Enemy.<br /> i.e. +1 difficulty for each drone appeared.<br /> However the above is not clearly defined in the ritual. Any suggestion or further guide available?<br /> <br /> thanks a lot<br /> JLW","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25452-dras76","name":"dras76","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T13:06:51-07:00","id":1509983,"title":"","content":"Mechanics for Wraiths and Spectres should be listed in the book (telling you the equivalent Discipline powers that will make it somewhat of a wraith)<br /> However if you want to add more richness to your story you can always make it a WtO crossover and actually use their appropriate powers from their book. Although that would require some readings if you are not familiar with WtO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T13:55:31-07:00","id":1509988,"title":"","content":"The ritual comes from the Telyavelic Tremere, summoning the drones of fallen tribal warriors; the remenants of soldiers' unfinished battles, revenge, obsession and etcetera. Drones are not sentient and are incapable of making judgements, they simply repeat the task they're obsessed over in this case, fighting the enemy they died fighting. In this case the ritual simply convinces the drone that somebody (tresspassers, pursuers, rivals, etc) is the target of this obsession.<br /> The drones will not act to defend the necromancer in any way except to target, harm and distract the vampire's appointed enemies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although they can not materialize fully in the physical world, they can use their own powers to hurl objects or frighten away attackers, in defense of the Necromancer. </div> </div> </div>I interpret this to mean that their available arcanos are Embody \u2022\u2022\u2022 and Outrage \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022.<br /> (Also I'm using Wr20 for this reference, as it's what I have on hand. Arcanoi were a little different in other editions)<br /> <br /> Embody \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> Can communicate in faint whispers. These are drones born of the regrets and obsessions of fallen warriors, so if they've got anything to say it's most likely going to be obsessive babbling and mantras about killing and defeating their enemies - they are liable to mistake their targets for the enemies they faced in life, unable to recognize that they're in a different situation.<br /> They can be seen as a &quot;hazy, translucent, and intangible apparition, only vaguely reminiscent of his mortal body&quot;. Ghouls and humans who witness it will go into a flight or fight response and be unable (and unwilling) to remember that they had any interaction with a ghost unless they're mediums, which is rare. Other exceptions are young children, and while I suppose you could decide a child is a threat to you in some reason, I feel like using this ritual against them is maybe a bit extreme?<br /> If they physically manifest then they can only stand there, unable to actually take any action; &quot;a gory recreation of his mortal shell at the time of his death, a luminous apparition with blazing, accusatory eyes, or any other manifestation that reflects a single strong emotion.&quot; Works for intimidation, or maybe blocking a doorway with a wall of bloodstained ghosts, but little else.<br /> <br /> Outrage \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> They can push things in a single, brief direction per push. Like pushing a vase off a windowsil.<br /> They can deliever blows to specific targets, both people and objects.<br /> They've got inhuman speed.<br /> And they can physically wield weapons and pick things up and throw them across the room.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T08:50:58-07:00","id":1510493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lirbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509970-necromancy-ritual-v20-masquerade?p=1509983#post1509983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanics for Wraiths and Spectres should be listed in the book (telling you the equivalent Discipline powers that will make it somewhat of a wraith)<br /> However if you want to add more richness to your story you can always make it a WtO crossover and actually use their appropriate powers from their book. Although that would require some readings if you are not familiar with WtO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I couldn't agree more. Vampire books in general have this tendency of downplaying the powers of Wraiths and Spectres in general and it ends up making players think they're no big deal. So, in this way many Necromantic powers become just a tool for intimidation that the players don't really take seriously (or more often, a tool for spying on others, etc.). I've seen many such cases over the course of more than 2 decades and half of storytelling. I feel they should list the powers that the Wraiths could use to affect the physical world and not let the powers be read so subjectively. Because as it is, players have a hard time taking seriously the threat the Wraiths could pose in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 05-02-2023, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T17:27:21-07:00","id":1510534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509970-necromancy-ritual-v20-masquerade?p=1510493#post1510493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I couldn't agree more. Vampire books in general have this tendency of downplaying the powers of Wraiths and Spectres in general and it ends up making players think they're no big deal. So, in this way many Necromantic powers become just a tool for intimidation that the players don't really take seriously (or more often, a tool for spying on others, etc.). I've seen many such cases over the course of more than 2 decades and half of storytelling. I feel they should list the powers that the Wraiths could use to affect the physical world and not let the powers be read so subjectively. Because as it is, players have a hard time taking seriously the threat the Wraiths could pose in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah you storytell for longer than I live \ud83d\ude02. Regardless yes I must say that players always look down at Necromancy because of that. But introducing actual wraiths can also be too powerful if the storyteller is not careful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T18:39:27-07:00","id":1510539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lirbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509970-necromancy-ritual-v20-masquerade?p=1510534#post1510534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Woah you storytell for longer than I live \ud83d\ude02. Regardless yes I must say that players always look down at Necromancy because of that. But introducing actual wraiths can also be too powerful if the storyteller is not careful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahaha how old are you, just out of curiosity? I started ST as a kid in any case, but it's been a long time since I started. And yes, we as Storytellers should always be careful to not let too much power in the PCs hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T01:06:44-07:00","id":1510574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509970-necromancy-ritual-v20-masquerade?p=1510539#post1510539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hahaha how old are you, just out of curiosity? I started ST as a kid in any case, but it's been a long time since I started. And yes, we as Storytellers should always be careful to not let too much power in the PCs hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>24, started when I was somewhere about 17 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}